1
00:02:15,882 --> 00:02:21,882
This time, the monsters are real!

2
00:04:31,764 --> 00:04:37,764
Scooby-Doo on Zombie Island is a animation, mystery,
family film directed by Jim Stenstrum.

3
00:06:47,647 --> 00:06:53,647
After going their separate ways, Scooby-Doo, Shaggy, Velma, Daphne, and Fred reunite to investigate the ghost of Moonscar the pirate
on a haunted bayou island, but it turns out the swashbuckler's spirit isn't the only creepy character on the island.

4
00:09:03,529 --> 00:09:09,529
The sleuths also meet up with cat creatures and zombies...

5
00:11:19,411 --> 00:11:25,411
and it looks like for the first time in their lives,
these ghouls might actually be real.

6
00:13:35,294 --> 00:13:41,294
Scooby-Doo (voice), played by Scott Innes.

7
00:15:51,176 --> 00:15:57,176
Shaggy Rogers (voice), played by Billy West.

8
00:18:07,058 --> 00:18:13,058
Daphne Blake (voice), played by Mary Kay Bergman.

9
00:20:22,941 --> 00:20:28,941
Fred Jones (voice), played by Frank Welker.

10
00:22:38,823 --> 00:22:44,823
Velma Dinkley (voice), played by B.J. Ward.

11
00:24:54,705 --> 00:25:00,705
Simone (voice), played by Adrienne Barbeau.

12
00:27:10,588 --> 00:27:16,588
Scooby-Doo on Zombie Island is a 1998 American direct-to-video animated
mystery comedy horror film based on the Scooby-Doo franchise.

13
00:29:26,470 --> 00:29:32,470
In the film, Shaggy, Scooby, Fred, Velma and Daphne reunite
after a year-long hiatus from Mystery, Inc.

14
00:31:42,352 --> 00:31:48,352
to investigate a bayou island said to be haunted by the
ghost of the pirate Morgan Moonscar.

15
00:33:58,235 --> 00:34:04,235
The film was directed by Jim Stenstrum and written by Glenn
Leopold, based on a story by Leopold and Davis Doi.

16
00:36:14,117 --> 00:36:20,117
Scooby-Doo's popularity had grown in the 1990s due
to reruns aired on Cartoon Network.

17
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
The channel's parent company, Time Warner, suggested developing
a direct-to-video (DTV) film on the property.

18
00:40:45,882 --> 00:40:51,882
The team at Hanna-Barbera, collaborating with Warner Bros.

19
00:43:01,764 --> 00:43:07,764
Animation (which was in the process of absorbing Hanna-Barbera at the
time), consisted of many veteran artists and writers.

20
00:45:17,647 --> 00:45:23,647
Many of the original voice actors of the series were replaced for the
film, although Frank Welker returned to voice Fred Jones.

21
00:47:33,529 --> 00:47:39,529
It was also the first of four Scooby-Doo direct-to-video films to be
animated overseas by Japanese animation studio Mook Animation.

22
00:49:49,411 --> 00:49:55,411
Rock bands Third Eye Blind and Skycycle contribute to the film's soundtrack.

23
00:52:05,294 --> 00:52:11,294
The film is dedicated to Don Messick, Scooby-Doo's
original voice actor who died in October 1997.

24
00:54:21,176 --> 00:54:27,176
Zombie Island contains a darker tone than most Scooby-Doo productions, and is notable for
containing real supernatural creatures rather than people in costumes.

25
00:56:37,058 --> 00:56:43,058
The film was released on September 22, 1998 and is notable for being the first Scooby-Doo production featuring the entire adult gang (sans
Scrappy-Doo) since The New Scooby-Doo Mysteries episode A Halloween Hassle at Dracula's Castle, which premiered on ABC on October 27, 1984.

26
00:58:52,941 --> 00:58:58,941
The film was aided by a $50 million promotional campaign, and
sponsorship deals with multiple companies.

27
01:01:08,823 --> 01:01:14,823
Sales of the film on VHS were high, and it became the first in
a long-running series of DTV Scooby-Doo films.

28
01:03:24,705 --> 01:03:30,705
The film made its first TV debut on October 31, 1998 on Cartoon Network.

29
01:05:40,588 --> 01:05:46,588
A sequel, Scooby-Doo!

30
01:07:56,470 --> 01:08:02,470
and the Witch's Ghost, was released in 1999, while two
decades after the film's release, Warner Bros.

31
01:10:12,352 --> 01:10:18,352
Animation developed a stand-alone sequel/retcon reboot Return to Zombie
Island from a different creative team, released in 2019.

32
01:12:28,235 --> 01:12:34,235
The film explores themes of new orleans, louisiana,
cartoon, haunted house, swamp, curse.

33
01:14:44,117 --> 01:14:50,117
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
